  "$comment": "How each realm's painted room is broken into layers (realm_layers.py, 2026-10-09). families: the room's lights, each keyed out by hue (fractions of the wheel; [h0, h1] wraps when h0 > h1) or 'hot' (near-white), saturation and value ramps, inside boxes [x0, y0, x1, y1] or ellipses {cx, cy, rx, ry} as fractions of the plate; each becomes its own additive layer the game drives on its own clock, and its light is taken out of the base. regions: parts of the painting cut out and set moving as loopable flipbooks - flow (lava, down a seam), flame (licks up), ripple (water), billow (cloud), sway (vines from the top, ferns from the bottom), shimmer (a sweep of light up ice), rays (light falling through a shaft). source 'plate' moves the painting itself (drawn over the base); 'family:<name>' moves that light (drawn added, at its family's level, and the static layer is cut out under it). Measured by eye on the paintings on a 10% grid.",
